+Many diagnostic processes are procedures that generate observations and diagnostic reports. In many cases, such an observation does not require an explicit representation of the procedure used to create the observation, but where there are details of interest about how the diagnostic procedure was performed, the <a href="procedure.html">Procedure</a> resource is used to describe the activity.
+</p>
+<p>
+The <a href="procedure-definitions.html#Procedure.outcome"><code>Procedure.outcome</code></a> element is for recording procedure effects (success, stent placed, reaction to contrast, etc.), not findings of evaluation procedures (lab results, radiology observations).
+</p>
 
 <p>
 In contrast to the <a href="observation.html">Observation</a> resource, the DiagnosticReport resource typically includes additional clinical context and some mix of atomic results, images, imaging reports, textual and coded interpretation, and formatted representations. Laboratory reports, pathology reports, and imaging reports should be represented using the DiagnosticReport resource. The Observation resource is used to represent individual, atomic measurements or assertions, regardless of whether they are generated by a clinical service, a device, or by the patient. The <a href="observation.html">Observation</a> resource is referenced by the DiagnosticReport to provide the atomic results for a particular investigation.
